  "processing_sequence": [
    "Read each byte-frozen raw PyVista PLY produced from the bound GridSDF using ImageData.contour(isosurfaces=[0.0], scalars=\"design_phi\"); independently attach source grid-cell IDs and require exact triangle-coordinate multiset agreement.",
    "Merge numerically exact coincident vertex coordinates with numpy.unique(axis=0); preserve every unique coordinate value.",
    "Remove exact duplicate triangles using sorted merged vertex IDs, retaining the earliest source triangle in input order.",
    "Remove triangles with repeated vertex indices and triangles whose float64 cross-product norm is exactly zero; report the two reasons separately.",
    "Partition remaining faces into deterministic edge-connected components ordered by first input face.",
    "For each face, evaluate the local trilinear GridSDF gradient at its centroid. Use floor-based half-open grid-cell selection, clamping only the outermost grid plane to the final cell. Flip that face iff dot(n, grad(phi)) is below -64*eps64*max(1, norm(grad(phi))). Leave roundoff-ambiguous faces unchanged and fail the gate if any remain. Never orient from signed volume.",
    "Write candidate PLY and Stage V STL with trimesh process=False; do not smooth, move vertices, fill holes, repair geometry, or alter the GridSDF."
  ],
  "purpose": "Qualify a deterministic, manifold, oriented Stage V surface export of the canonical v17 GridSDF zero-level geometry without changing vertex coordinates or the signed-distance field.",
